course: dictionary
lesson: 2188
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word costume can mean special clothes for pretending, the clothes actors wear, the clothes of a country or a time in history, or a swimsuit. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «Freddie wore his pirate costume to the party» tells you costume means clothes worn to look like someone else.
explain: Look at the clues again when the meaning changes. «The actors changed costume between the scenes» is about clothes worn in a play. «Pack your costume, we're going swimming» is about a swimsuit, because of the word swimming. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence to check it. Put «swimsuit» in place of costume in «Pack your costume, we're going swimming». It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A costume is a set of special clothes worn to look like someone or something else, such as a pirate costume.
fact: A costume can also be the clothes worn by actors in a play or film.
fact: A costume can mean the clothes typical of a country or a time in history, such as Victorian costume.
fact: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a swimming costume is a swimsuit. In Australia people often say «cozzie».
fact: Halloween costumes should let you see well and be seen in the dark, so add reflective tape or carry a torch, and keep well away from candles.
exercise: «Freddie wore a pirate costume to the party.» What is a costume here? | *A set of special clothes worn to look like someone else | A type of party food | A kind of boat | A school timetable
exercise: «The actors changed costume between the scenes.» Who wears a costume in this sentence? | Shop workers at the till | Pupils on the bus | Farmers in the fields | *Actors in a play
exercise: «Pack your costume, we're going swimming.» What does costume mean here? | A type of cloak | *A swimsuit | A pirate hat | A school uniform
test: «Her costume for the school play was a long blue dress from Victorian times.» Which meaning of costume fits best? | A swimsuit | *Clothes typical of a time in history | A type of party food | A set of clothes to look like a pirate
test: Why is it useful to check your meaning by putting it into the sentence? | It makes the sentence longer | It tells you how to spell the word | *It shows whether the meaning still makes sense | It replaces the whole sentence
exam: «Vikings did not wear horned helmets in battle; the horns come from costumes made for an opera in 1876.» What does costume mean here? | The clothes typical of a country in history | A swimsuit | A set of clothes worn to look like a pirate | *Clothes worn by actors in a play
